the coronavirus is forcing all of us to  protect ourselves from germs  and that means more masks gloves and  wipes but it also means more trash  laura podesta explains how our personal  protective equipment could hurt the  environment  a byproduct of the coronavirus crisis is  this trash problem  it definitely grosses me out to see all  that  trash that you know who knows what germs  it has on it  discarded sanitizer bottles gloves and  face masks often end up on the streets  creating both a biohazard and an  environmental hazard  no one wants to touch ppe litter right  so people are afraid that it's  contaminated  so that means they're not picking it up  from the streets mark benfield is a  professor in the department of  oceanography at louisiana state  university  he's been tracking ppe litter around the  country since the pandemic began  benfield says masks or gloves washing  into sewers is a major  concern they'll end up in our waterways  where the plastic can break down  and eventually be ingested by small  aquatic animals  if a human being eats a fish that's  consumed lots of smaller animals  then those pollutants can get into our  bodies  to combat the problem the mayor of  houston recently launched an  anti-litter campaign called don't let  houston go to waste  the city will hold cleanup events that  will target illegal dumping  and in los angeles anyone caught  dropping a mask or glove  could be fined 250 bucks but many are  finding the solution lies with our  choices  like wearing a reusable mask these  things are  run like 20 bucks a pop so i'm not going  to throw it on the ground anywhere  others say they're speaking out and i  say something  all the time like can you pick that up  garbage cans right there  and gently reminding their neighbors the  location of the nearest trash can  laura podesta cbs news new york  in new york city staff are trying to  educate the public about ppe waste  they've started posting reminders about  proper disposal near hospitals bus  stations and grocery stores to try and  help
 

